lemma[fact] L32:gideon-embezzled-escrow-17-funds-knew-before-october "Gideon embezzled the Escrow 17 funds and knew before October 18 that Aldous intended to expose the discrepancies."
  <- AND#J71(L53, P99)

lemma[fact] L33:evidence-supports-conclusion-that-gideon-prepared-poisoned-clasp "The evidence supports the conclusion that Gideon prepared the poisoned clasp mechanism and thereby killed Aldous."
  <- AND#J72(L57, L56)

lemma[fact] L34:vesper-psalter-was-false-object-aldous-collection-that "The Vesper Psalter was the false object in Aldous's collection that he intended to expose."
  <- AND#J73(L58, L59)

lemma[fact] L35:escrow-17-was-false-account-aldous-ledger-that "Escrow 17 was the false account in Aldous's ledger that he intended to expose."
  <- AND#J74(L60, P47)

lemma[fact] L36:gideon-killed-ruth-aldous-conceal-escrow-17-embezzlement "Gideon killed Ruth and Aldous to conceal the Escrow 17 embezzlement, while Beatrice's forged Vesper Psalter was the separate false object."
  <- AND#J75(L61, L62)

lemma[fact] L37:escrow-17-records-supposed-payments-march-rowe-after "Escrow 17 records supposed payments to March & Rowe after that firm had ceased trading."
  <- AND#J37(P69, P79, P80)

lemma[fact] L38:identical-escrow-17-authorizations-were-produced-aldous-signature "The identical Escrow 17 authorizations were produced with Aldous's signature stamp rather than separately written signatures."
  <- AND#J38(P81, P82)

lemma[fact] L39:escrow-17-withdrawals-have-no-corresponding-acquisitions-no "The Escrow 17 withdrawals have no corresponding acquisitions and no traced destination within the estate."
  <- AND#J39(P78, P84, P85)

lemma[fact] L40:gideon-retained-duplicate-poison-cabinet-key-that-aldous "Gideon retained the duplicate poison-cabinet key that Aldous had borrowed."
  <- AND#J40(P90, P25)

lemma[fact] L41:aconitine-disappeared-locked-cabinet-after-its-recorded-presence "The aconitine disappeared from the locked cabinet after its recorded presence on September 30."
  <- AND#J41(P22, P23)

lemma[fact] L42:after-seeing-ruth-row-17-note-gideon-could "After seeing Ruth's Row 17 note, Gideon could have confused it with the similarly numbered Escrow 17 account."
  <- AND#J42(P96, P50, P77)

lemma[fact] L43:evidence-connects-gideon-private-use-estate-office-typewriter "The evidence connects Gideon's private use of the estate-office typewriter to the forged summons directing Ruth to bring her notes."
  <- AND#J43(P93, P94)

lemma[fact] L44:gideon-had-direct-financial-interest-preventing-discovery-escrow "Gideon had a direct financial interest in preventing discovery of Escrow 17."
  <- AND#J44(P83, P92)

lemma[fact] L45:gideon-had-reason-believe-ruth-row-17-notes "Gideon had reason to believe Ruth's Row 17 notes threatened to expose his Escrow 17 interests."
  <- AND#J45(L42, L44)

lemma[fact] L46:clasp-contained-needle-that-projected-through-slender-groove "The clasp contained a needle that projected through the slender groove and then retracted into the spine."
  <- AND#J46(P8, P9, P109)

lemma[fact] L47:gideon-had-private-access-estate-office-typewriter-used "Gideon had private access to the estate-office typewriter used to address Aldous's parcel shortly before delivery."
  <- AND#J47(P113, P114)

lemma[fact] L48:parcel-was-delivered-after-old-march-rowe-labels "The parcel was delivered after old March & Rowe labels were available within Vesper House."
  <- AND#J48(P10, P70)

lemma[fact] L49:clasp-puncture-mechanism-could-kill-after-delay-during "The clasp's puncture mechanism could kill after a delay during which its victim remained capable of speaking."
  <- AND#J49(P67, L26)

lemma[fact] L50:ruth-was-struck-freight-siding-after-injuries-consistent "Ruth was struck at a freight siding after injuries consistent with a struggle and forceful push."
  <- AND#J50(P73, P115)

lemma[fact] L51:ruth-impaired-nighttime-vision-unused-return-ticket-are "Ruth's impaired nighttime vision and unused return ticket are inconsistent with an intended death at the siding."
  <- AND#J51(P74, P75)

lemma[fact] L52:ruth-homicide-involved-struggle-that-left-physical-evidence "Ruth's homicide involved a struggle that left physical evidence from Gideon's overcoat in her hand."
  <- AND#J52(L30, P95)

lemma[fact] L53:gideon-controlled-personally-benefited-fraud-indicated-escrow-17 "Gideon controlled and personally benefited from the fraud indicated by Escrow 17."
  <- AND#J53(L14, P83, P92)

lemma[fact] L54:gideon-had-access-both-missing-poison-unique-design "Gideon had access both to the missing poison and to the unique design used in the fatal clasp."
  <- AND#J54(L17, L27)

lemma[fact] L55:gideon-had-advance-warning-opportunity-consistent-preparing-parcel "Gideon had advance warning and an opportunity consistent with preparing the parcel before delivery."
  <- AND#J55(L22, L28)

lemma[fact] L56:delayed-clasp-mechanism-killed-aldous-despite-gideon-presence "The delayed clasp mechanism killed Aldous despite Gideon's presence in the billiard room at the time of collapse."
  <- AND#J56(L26, L29)

lemma[fact] L57:gideon-had-means-preparation-opportunity-financial-motive-poisoned "Gideon had the means, preparation opportunity, and financial motive for the poisoned-parcel murder."
  <- AND#J57(L54, L55, L32)

lemma[fact] L58:suspicious-object-row-17-was-beatrice-forged-vesper "The suspicious object in Row 17 was Beatrice's forged Vesper Psalter."
  <- AND#J58(P50, P52, P58)

lemma[fact] L59:aldous-possessed-ruth-evidence-before-announcing-that-object "Aldous possessed Ruth's evidence before announcing that an object in his collection was false."
  <- AND#J59(P46, P91)

